  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - God bless your work today. Stay strong!
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "Keep your chin up. I\u2019ll mention you in my thoughts tonight."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Whatever happens next, know that you did your duty. Peace be with you.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "If this is where I\u2019m needed most, then this is where I\u2019ll stay."
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "Do the others in there need someone to talk to? I\u2019m ready."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - A small room is a perfect place for a big prayer. I don't mind.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "Oh... so... it\u2019s time... already..."
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I forgive... you... please... don't carry... this weight...
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - The light... is finally... breaking... through...
  quarantineExitLines:
  - Then let this be my cell and my ministry both. There are souls here who need
    tending.
  - "Brother, whatever I carry \u2014 let it stay in here with me, away from the
    others."
  - God gives us the walls we need, not the walls we want. I can work with this.
  killExitLines:
  - "I only ask\u2026 that you carry this gently\u2026 It is a heavy thing to carry\u2026"
  - "If this was your duty\u2026 then may God\u2026 grant you peace\u2026 for it\u2026"
  - "Lord\u2026 receive me\u2026 I tried\u2026 I tried to do enough\u2026"
  voiceAudioClips: []
  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: a2487dfb69806694d9657932307e14e3, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The cathedral on the hill. I was leading evening prayers.
    midDaysAnswer: I've been moving between parishes. The need is everywhere now.
    finalDaysAnswer: I was giving last rites. There are many to give.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The market district. Small errands. Nothing that required
      the cloth. Just a man doing his shopping.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Home. I rested today. The parishes are managing well.
      They don't need me for every small thing.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The cathedral. Evening prayers. A very peaceful service.
      Quiet congregation. Nothing unusual.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The spirit is willing. The body is what it is.
    midDaysAnswer: I have a tremor in my left hand. I hide it when I can.
    finalDaysAnswer: I have stopped asking that question. It doesn't seem important
      now.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: I feel strong. Both in body and spirit. No complaints.
      I am grateful for that.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No tremor. My hands are perfectly steady. I lift the chalice
      with both every morning. No difficulty.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: I feel better than I have in years. Clear and present.
      I am very much here. Very much myself.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The seminary brothers. A full house.
    midDaysAnswer: Two brothers remain. The others have gone to serve elsewhere.
    finalDaysAnswer: No one now. I tend the church alone.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Alone. The rectory has been empty for some time now.
      I find peace in the quiet.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: All the brothers, still a full house. No one has left.
      We pray together every evening as always.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The brothers are still there. A full house. Nothing
      has changed. Father Dmitri was at breakfast this morning.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Hello, brother. It is a grim morning, but we are still here, are we not?
    - You look tired, officer. I will mention you in my prayers tonight. I mean that.
    - Someone has to hold the line. I am glad it is a person like you.
    midDays:
    - The ash is getting into everything, even the pews. We keep the doors open anyway.
    - I saw the look in people's eyes today. They need more than bread right now.
    - Take the ID. I have a dozen more families to check on before curfew.
    finalDays:
    - I am going back into the smog. There are people alone out there who need a
      voice.
    - The bells are cracked but the message is the same. We are not abandoned.
    - Use your stamp, brother. Let us finish this chapter so we can see what is on
      the next page.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
  IDNumber: 6328957
